["15:17"]={"“You can take the \0033:17\004 to Peterborough, where you’ll have to change and catch the 4:09 for Doncaster, then change again. You’ll arrive in Hull at 6:32.”","Dougie Mortimer’s Right Arm","Jeffrey Archer"},
["15:18"]={"The graphic film is already wrinkling: the eagle has a broken wing; the hour hand is kinked. It is \003eighteen minutes past three\004.","Fairyland","Paul J. McAuley"},
["15:19"]={"At \003nineteen minutes past three\004 Cecily Thorogood, still self-possessed, but no longer very prettily clad, was submerged in the chilly Atlantic up to her shoulders and clinging to the life-line of an upturned jolly-boat.","The Long Trick","Lewis Anselm da Costa Ritchie"},
["15:20"]={"James jammed his trilby over his ears, looked the other way and passed the time by chatting to Sam O’Flaherty about the \0033:20\004, the King George VI and Queen Elizabeth Stakes.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["15:21"]={"\0033:21 P.M.\004\n“Let them go,” Ramirez said. “We have what we need.” He bent down and picked up the box.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["15:22"]={"Ruth finally walked through the door at \0033:22 P.M.\004 “Any messages?” she asked the receptionist.\n“No,” replied the girl, “but there is a lady waiting to see you.”","False Impression","Jeffrey Archer"},
["15:23"]={"\003Three twenty-three\004! Is that all? Doesn’t time — no, I’ve already said that, thought that. I sit and watch the seconds change on the watch. I used to have a limited edition Rolex worth the price of a new car but I lost it.","Espedair Street","Iain Banks"},
["15:24"]={"The organist, in his incredulous relief, made a horrible mess of the first bars of the wedding march. It was \003twenty-four minutes past three\004 before Jimmy mouthed the first sentence of the day that even he was unable to shorten.\n“I do,” he said.","The Reginald Perrin Omnibus","David Nobbs"},
["15:25"]={"The next afternoon Mr. Underhill finished at the office early and took the three o’clock train, arriving out in Green Town at \003three twenty-five\004, in plenty of time to drink in the brisk rays of the autumnal sun.","The Playground","Ray Bradbury"},
["15:26"]={"It was almost \00315:26\004 so I sent a two-word message to Chris — “All OK” — then started walking purposefully towards the nearest Portakabin, trying not to dwell too much on the insanity of what I was doing.","The Witness","Simon Kernick"},
["15:27"]={"And she rang the Reverend Peters and he came into school at \0033:27 p.m.\004 and he said, “So, young man, are we ready to roll?”","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["15:28"]={"“\003Three twenty-eight\004!” he cried, excitedly. “Didn’t I tell you! Who says we can’t keep time up here! She’ll run her plank ashore at three forty-five to the dot!”","The Woman from Outside","Hulbert Footner"},
["15:29"]={"\0033:29 P.M.\004\nEvents were getting serious enough that the operation had been moved down to the Situation Room, in the White House basement.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["15:30"]={"There wasn’t the faintest trace of writing on any of them, not even Auntie Mabel’s Birthday, or dentist, \003half-past three\004.","Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets","J.K. Rowling"},
["15:31"]={"At \003three-thirty one and a half\004 by my wrist watch—the only piece of jewelry, by the way, you’ve left me—I received, Lord Tawdry, this communication from the hospital cot of the Honorable Bertram Butternut!","The Shriek: A Satirical Burlesque","Charles Somerville"},
["15:32"]={"At \0033:32\004 precisely, I noticed Kaitlyn striding confidently past the Wok House. She saw me the moment I raised my hand, flashed her very white and newly straightened teeth at me, and headed over.","The Fault in Our Stars","John Green"},
["15:33"]={"I picked up my briefcase, glancing at my watch again as I did so. \003Three thirty-three\004.","11/22/63","Stephen King"},
["15:34"]={"It was \00315:34\004 now and the sleepiness felt like lead inside him.","Devil’s Peak","Deon Meyer"},
["15:35"]={"If Me flashed a little crazy after a restless night of smoking & prowling the darkened house with owl-eyes alert to suspicious noises outside & on the roof, it didn’t inevitably mean she’d still be in such a state when the schoolbus deposited Wolfie back home at \0033:35 P.M.\004","I Am No One You Know: Stories","Joyce Carol Oates"},
["15:36"]={"Meanwhile a girl was standing in an airport concourse. A big clock suspended from the ceiling said it was \003twenty-four minutes to four\004.","The Intruders","Michael Marshall"},
["15:37"]={"The explosion was now officially designated an “Act of God”. But, thought Dirk, what god? And why? What god would be hanging around Terminal Two of Heathrow Airport trying to catch the \00315:37\004 flight to Oslo?","The Long Dark Tea-Time of the Soul","Douglas Adams"},
